 "title": "When a contact shared by two processes binds them at the first step",
 "subject": "Shared contacts between two rings, read with the canonical knot test on their space-time law, at lag 1 and in the linear case",
 "conclusion": "Two rings sharing one contact cell are bound by it at lag 1 exactly when its combiner is XOR or XNOR and neither ring rule is canalizing at its centre, and a self-blind contact binds at lag 1 exactly when its 4 x 4 table has no constant row or column (22,874 of 65,536 laws). With linear or affine rings and an affine contact law the contact binds at lag T exactly when its row of M^T meets both rings.",
